hostname internet
!
ip routing
!
! ============================================================
! internet — simulated upstream provider, NOT in OSPF
!
! Topology: [core] --OSPF area 0-- [asbr] --NOT in OSPF-- [internet]
!
! internet represents the upstream ISP or internet gateway.
! It runs NO OSPF. It simply provides a target for the default route
! that asbr will inject into the OSPF domain.
!
! internet needs a return route toward the internal network
! if you want end-to-end ping to work.
! ============================================================

interface Loopback0
 ip address 10.99.0.1/32

! Link to asbr — segment 203.0.113.0/30 — NOT in OSPF
! asbr is .1, internet is .2
interface Ethernet1
 no switchport
 description Link to asbr (203.0.113.0/30, asbr=.1 internet=.2) — no OSPF
 ip address 203.0.113.2/30

! ============================================================
! internet has NO OSPF configuration.
!
! To test end-to-end reachability (core -> internet):
!   1. Configure OSPF on core and asbr (Steps 1-3 in asbr's frr.conf)
!   2. core should have: O*E2 0.0.0.0/0 via 10.1.12.2 (asbr's Ethernet1 IP)
!   3. Add a return route on internet so replies can get back:
!      In vtysh on internet:
!        ip route 10.0.0.0/8 203.0.113.1
!   4. From core, ping internet's loopback:
!        ping 10.99.0.1 source 10.0.0.1
!
! To simulate internet going down (test conditional default):
!   On the lab host (bash):
!     sudo docker exec clab-ospf-default-route-internet ip link set Ethernet1 down
!   Watch asbr lose the 203.0.113.0/30 route.
!   If route-map condition is configured, asbr should stop advertising default.
!   core's O*E2 default should disappear within the OSPF dead interval.
! ============================================================
